== 1. Frequently Asked Student Questions (FAQs)
#faq-item(
  q: "Why can't CPU manufacturers just build a 10.0 GHz processor?",
  a: "The Power Wall: Power consumption and heat dissipation increase exponentially with voltage and frequency ($P approx C V^2 f$). At 10 GHz, silicon produces so much heat that conventional copper coolers cannot prevent thermal destruction!"
)
#faq-item(
  q: "What is the difference between Program Counter (PC) and Instruction Register (IR)?",
  a: "The PC holds the MEMORY ADDRESS of the next instruction waiting to be fetched from RAM. The IR holds the ACTUAL BINARY OPWORD of the current instruction while it is being decoded and executed."
)
#faq-item(
  q: "What is the role of Hyper-Threading / Simultaneous Multithreading (SMT)?",
  a: "SMT duplicates architectural registers so a single physical CPU core presents itself to the OS as two logical cores, allowing idle execution pipelines to process a second instruction stream simultaneously."
)

#v(2pt)

== 2. Short-Answer Review Questions with Verified Answers
#short-qa(
  num: 1,
  q: "Name the two primary functional units within the CPU Control Unit.",
  a: "The Instruction Decoder (translates binary opcodes) and the Timing and Control Logic (generates clock synchronization pulses)."
)
#short-qa(
  num: 2,
  q: "What happens to the Program Counter (PC) register immediately after an instruction is fetched?",
  a: "The PC is automatically incremented by the instruction word length (e.g. +4 bytes in 32-bit/64-bit architectures) to point to the subsequent instruction address."
)
#short-qa(
  num: 3,
  q: "Define IPC and state how modern superscalar processors achieve IPC greater than 1.",
  a: "Instructions Per Cycle: Modern CPUs achieve IPC > 1 by deploying multiple parallel execution units (multiple ALUs, FPUs) and out-of-order execution pipelines."
)
#short-qa(
  num: 4,
  q: "What is the purpose of the Flag Register (Program Status Word)?",
  a: "It holds 1-bit status indicators (Zero, Carry, Sign, Overflow) reflecting the mathematical outcome of the most recent ALU operation for conditional branching."
)

#v(2pt)

